Package: gambitR3D
Title: Multilevel Chess: Play, Analyse and Train
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Raban", "Heller", email = "raban.heller@uni-ulm.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742")),
    person("three.js authors", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "bundled three.js library, see inst/app/www/vendor/PROVENANCE.md")
  )
Description: An experimental multilevel chess variant on three fixed four by
    four boards and four movable two by two platforms, with 64 physical
    squares that keep their identity when platforms move. Provides an
    authoritative rules engine with a versioned and hashed rules profile, a
    lossless native game format, an alpha-beta search opponent, a local
    'SQLite' game database, game and collection analysis with reproducible
    plots and reports, a 'Shiny' application with synchronised 2D and 3D
    views, evidence-grounded coaching and practice, and an optional isolated
    'PyTorch' worker for training and playing a small transformer. The rules
    are a transparent project convention, not an official rulebook. A
    companion to 'gambitR'.
